  note pages, 390 wide, motion on: the page's guide lines with "same scale": "A generated player drafted the same year at your position. He plays his own seasons on the same scale you do, can win a ring before you and retire before you, and the head to head is kept for good. He is fictional, like your own player, so no real player's career is being simulated."
  note pages, 390 wide, motion on: the "?" lines that name the rival: "Read the News box. The paper writes up every season in your own position's stat, the SocialGram shows followers read off your fanbase with three fan comments under the latest post, and the rival's card keeps the head to head against the player drafted the same" / "MAKING THE CALL WHEN YOUR RIVAL FORCES ONE" / "Some seasons your rival hands you a decision instead of a headline: a flagrant you can answer or let go, a debate show offering real money, a youth camp his foundation wants you to co-host, an All-Star vote his team is buying ads for. Every button prints exact" / "How your rival's choices work" / "A season where your rival makes no headline has a 45% shot at a rival choice instead, never both in the same year, and every choice shows up once before any of them repeats. The buttons move only what they print: morale, fanbase, net worth, karma or the heat o" / "Answering your rival's flagrant" / "Your rival takes you out on a drive and the refs upgrade it to a flagrant. Give it right back heats the feud and usually pays Morale +8, but it carries a 30% chance you are the one who gets tossed (Morale -5, Fanbase -5, Net worth -$100k). Help him up on camer" / "Who is my rival?" / "Read the News box. The paper writes up every season in your own position's stat, the SocialGram shows followers read off your fanbase with three fan comments under the latest post, and the rival's card keeps the head to head against the player drafted the same" / "Some seasons your rival hands you a decision instead of a headline: a flagrant you can answer or let go, a debate show offering real money, a youth camp his foundation wants you to co-host, an All-Star vote his team is buying ads for. Every button prints exact" / "A season where your rival makes no headline has a 45% shot at a rival choice instead, never both in the same year, and every choice shows up once before any of them repeats. The buttons move only what 